<p>A professional blow-dry starts with proper preparation of the hair. Product choice, temperature control and the way of working are adapted to each hair type for the most natural result. Fine hair needs a technique that creates more fullness, while thick or heavy hair needs a different approach so the waves stay light and lasting.</p>
<p>Just as important is the way the waves fall. Instead of sharp breaks and overly defined strands, the goal is a soft, natural shape that follows the movement of the hair. When the blow-dry is done properly, hair looks groomed, keeps its volume and is easy to refresh through the day.</p>
<p>The final result is also affected by hair length, the shape of the cut and its natural texture. That is why the same wave style will not be done the same way on everyone, but the technique is adapted for the most natural result.</p>
